| Concept     | Order matters? | Formula |
| ----------- | -------------- | ------- |
| Permutation | Yes            |         |
| Combination | No             |         |
| Subsets     | No             |         |

### 7\. ICPC quick decision guide

| Problem says...                    | Think about                |
| ---------------------------------- | -------------------------- |
| Arrange elements                   | next_permutation()         |
| Choose exactly K elements          | Combination                |
| Generate all subsets               | Bitmask                    |
| Choose items with constraints      | Backtracking               |
| Select teams/groups                | Combination                |
| All possible selections with order | Permutation                |
| Count ways to choose               |                            |
| Optimize a selection               | DP / Greedy / Backtracking |

### 8\. Useful C++ combination calculation

Avoid calculating factorials directly for large `n`.

```cpp
long long nCr(int n, int r) {

    if (r > n) return 0;

    r = min(r, n - r);

    long long ans = 1;

    for (int i = 1; i <= r; i++) {
        ans = ans * (n - i + 1) / i;
    }

    return ans;
}
```

This is suitable when the intermediate multiplication fits in `long long`. For very large constraints, use modular arithmetic or another appropriate method.

